143 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 96 0 R
/E ( Over the past decade, higher educational institutions globally have witnessed a seismic shift in student behaviour, particularly concerning the use of digital technologies. Where previous generations of students faced relatively discrete boundaries between leisure and study, contemporary undergraduates carry with them, at virtually all times, devices that provide instant access to a rich ecosystem of social, informational, and entertainment content. The smartphone has effectively collapsed the boundary between study space and social space, and social media platforms have been the primary beneficiaries of this collapse.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
