/E (The questionnaire comprised 19 items across two sections. Section 1 collected demographic information \(age group, gender\). Section 2 measured social media behaviour and its consequences through 17 items covering daily usage hours, frequency of use during study, focus reduction, procrastination, coursework distraction, time management difficulty, notification disruption, multitasking, study delay, usage-limitation attempts, platform preference, academic performance impact frequency, productivity when avoiding social media, break frequency, and overall academic productivity impact. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
