277 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 110 0 R
/E (Several limitations merit acknowledgement. First, the sample \(n = 50\) is modest, reducing statistical power for detecting small effects. The marginal finding for H3 \(p = 0.074\) may reflect a true relationship that remains undetected due to sample size. Second, the study relies entirely on self-report measures, which are subject to social desirability bias. Third, the gender imbalance \(78% female\) limits generalisability of gender-related findings. Fourth, all significant findings are correlational; the cross-sectional design precludes causal inference)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
