820 0 obj
<<
/Title (The study is structured as follows. Section 2 presents a comprehensive review of the theoretical and empirical literature, organised around the key mechanisms of interest: social media and academic performance, procrastination as a mediating mechanism, attention fragmentation and focus reduction, and platform-specific and gender effects. Section 3 articulates the six study hypotheses. Section 4 describes the research design, sampling strategy, survey instrument, variable operationalisation, and data analysis plan. Section 5 presents the results across descriptive statistics, hypothesis tests, extended correlation analysis, regression models, and group comparisons. Section 6 discusses the findings in theoretical and practical context. Sections 7 and 8 address policy implications and conclusions)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 818 0 R
/Next 822 0 R
>>
endobj
